      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I totally agree with this assessment. While I am not too fond at all with how this system is being implemented based on what has been show so far, a lot of concern could be assuaged through these suggestions. Personally I do not like that a user's trust level is so obvious to others. There is no real, practical reason to have to know what a user's rank is that I can think of that would require that information to be so blatant, such as with nameplate colours. This system will certainly lead to elitism, which I believe the vrchat team is already aware of in some capacity, given that high tiered users can hide the fact they are so. I would suggest that everyone's names remain the same colour as they are now. Also the default settings for mid tier users seem very extreme to me, given that the public are not aware of how the trust system is actually applied per user. Many friends of mine would have their particles and shaders blocked by default even with hundreds of hours in-game and no infractions, which honestly seems ridiculous.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
