      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Agree, and also problem is not only in naming. This system already used by beta-testers and almost all my friends and ppl I meet in worlds are enabled this, so lower ranks like visitor or new user are block by default for almost everyone. Just imagine you're newbie, you joing worlds, meeting ppl but they all block you. You are not intresing for anyone and you should find another newbies in this huge dimension to make friends and try to understand concept of this game alone. You're not socilalized. This was a problem even before trust system: when a lot of cheaters and hackers became active in winter, alot of ppl migreated from publics into privates forming own closed societies, who are suspicious of all newcomers and strangers. This created some of segregation between \"the olds\" and \"the news\" in vrc: publics turn into trash with cheaters, hackers, abusers, raiders, and... newbies that truing to understand wtf is going on. Going to public was like a sub-game where you going into wild west where your avatars can be stolen and you game is crashed. I am 100% VRC lost a lot of audience just because ppl treat this game like a shit while seeing that unfriendly enviroment.\nSo.\nTrust system officially confirms this way of VR life, tagging everyone as a criminals who should prove that they are not criminals. That's sad and terrifying.\n\nI know that because I made the world Khrushchyovka and put important keywords into it's description so when new russian joins the game and trying to (literaly) search other russians they see my world in search and they going to it. I saw hundreds if not thousends of newbies and they all was shocked by trash is going on and asking \"where the hell is all normal ppl?\"",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
