  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "By marking an icon in the player's menu as \"safety\" and having higher ranks be known as \"trusted\", the system is subtextually saying to new players that they aren't safe, and they aren't trusted. No player in their right mind would intentionally want to make themselves less safe, and what the menu is essentially saying is that you aren't truly safe in VRChat until everyone is a mute defaultmat Ybot torso. \n\nSimply renaming it to \"filters\" and removing the shield would fix this issue, and perhaps coming up with a new name in lieu of \"trusted\", and perhaps ditch the subtitles altogether in favor of nameplate colors that are expounded upon when you click the player, since seeing that someone is a \"known user\" isn't really necessary and it adds to the visual noise in crowded rooms.",
